<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adaptive TTS decides how much reasoning a query needs but treats the cost of a sample as fixed, while inference and energy systems manage the GPU but do not change how much reasoning each query gets.
On a shared GPU, these decisions depend on each other: one more sample is worth it only if the answers so far and the current GPU cost justify it.
No prior method in Table <a href="#S2.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ II-C Research Gap ‣ II Background and Related Work ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a> reads the live GPU state; the closest, Adaptive-Cal <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, uses offline-calibrated models.
<span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span> makes this decision at runtime using both signals, and <span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online learns the cost online without per-dataset profiling.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Motivation</span></h2>

<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2610.25519v1/figures/fig_motivation.png" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/214;" width="476" height="214" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 3: </span>Motivation. (a) Energy per answered query for a fixed budget of <math id="S3.F3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=4</annotation></semantics></math> at four GPU load levels, relative to idle. The value under each level is the measured GPU utilization. (b) Error of the offline cost model, averaged over four datasets. Without live GPU state (Adaptive-Cal), the error grows from 26% at idle to 283% at high load. Adding live GPU state (<span id="S3.F3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated) lowers the high-load error to 55%, but the error is still large at medium load (130%).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When several jobs share one GPU, they compete for the same compute units, memory bandwidth, and power limit.
As a result, the same microbatch runs longer, and the GPU draws more power while it runs.
In our setup, each microbatch is charged for the GPU energy used while it occupies the GPU (§<a href="#S6" title="VI Experimental Methodology ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI</span></a>), so the same number of samples costs more joules when the GPU is busy.
This cost depends on the current load, which changes over time and is not known in advance.
Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ III Motivation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows two observations from our experiments.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observation 1: the same budget can cost several times more.</span>
With a fixed budget of <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=4</annotation></semantics></math>, the energy per answered query rises with load on all four datasets.
At high load it is 3.7<math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> the idle value on GSM8K and MATH, and 4.1<math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> on ARC-Challenge.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Observation 2: an offline cost model does not follow the load.</span>
A cost model fitted offline predicts the cost of a budget before it runs.
Fig. <a href="#S3.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ III Motivation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(b) shows that its prediction error grows quickly as the GPU becomes busy.
Adding the live GPU state as an input helps, but it does not remove the problem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These observations lead to four design goals for a TTS controller on a shared GPU:</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">G1 – Spend samples where they help.</span> Give more samples only to queries whose answer is still uncertain.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">G2 – Follow the live cost.</span> Use the cost of a sample <em id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">now</em>, not the cost measured during profiling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">G3 – Avoid expensive profiling.</span> Do not require a new offline calibration for every dataset.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">G4 – Stay safe and serve everyone.</span> Never exceed the energy budget, and avoid deferring queries.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated meets G1, partly meets G2, and does not meet G3.
<span id="S3.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online is designed to meet all four.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Problem Formulation</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We serve a stream of <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> queries <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{1},\dots,q_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{1},\dots,q_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> on one GPU that is shared with other jobs.
For each query <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the controller chooses a budget <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}\in\mathcal{B}=\{1,3,4,6,8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}\in\mathcal{B}=\{1,3,4,6,8\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The GPU condition at time <math id="S4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Because <math id="S4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> changes, the same budget can have a different energy cost at different times.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All queries share one energy budget <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the measured GPU energy used for query <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The total must stay within the budget:</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}E_{i}\leq E_{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}E_{i}\leq E_{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">A query is admitted only if its predicted cost fits its share of the remaining budget, <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\mathrm{rem}}/N_{\mathrm{rem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>rem</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>rem</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\mathrm{rem}}/N_{\mathrm{rem}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathrm{rem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>rem</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathrm{rem}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of queries left; otherwise it is <em id="S4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">deferred</em>.
A deferred query gets no answer, and we write <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
The <em id="S4.p2.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">defer rate</em> is the fraction of deferred queries, and the <em id="S4.p2.2.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">service coverage</em> is one minus the defer rate. The goal is to answer as many queries correctly as possible while keeping Eq. (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In IV Problem Formulation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>):</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{B_{1},\dots,B_{N}}\ \sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}\big[\text{answer to }q_{i}\text{ is correct}\big]\quad\text{s.t. Eq.~\eqref{eq:budget}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mtext>answer to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is correct</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>s.t. Eq. (</mtext><mtext><a href="#S4.E1" title="In IV Problem Formulation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{B_{1},\dots,B_{N}}\ \sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbf{1}\big[\text{answer to }q_{i}\text{ is correct}\big]\quad\text{s.t. Eq.~\eqref{eq:budget}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">A deferred query counts as not correct.
So deferring is never free: it protects the budget, but it lowers accuracy and coverage.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATESTDesign</span></h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">V-A</span> </span><span id="S5.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Overview</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span> has two modes that share the same budget ladder, GPU monitor (NVML <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>), and energy accounting.
They differ in <em id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">when</em> they decide and <em id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">what they learn</em>.
The default mode, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online, decides step by step, using the samples it has already generated and a cost model that it learns while it runs.
The offline mode, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated, decides the whole budget once, before generating any sample, using models built offline.
Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ V-A Overview ‣ V ATESTDesign ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a> summarizes the differences.</p>
</div>
