<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">When to use the offline mode.</span>
<span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online is the right choice when the load changes or new models and datasets arrive often.
<span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated is useful in three cases: (1) the model, GPU, and workload stay the same long enough to reuse one profile, where it reaches higher accuracy under stable load (§<a href="#S7.SS6" title="VII-F Q6: When Does Offline Calibration Win? ‣ VII Evaluation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VII-F</span></a>); (2) the service needs low tail latency or high throughput on short tasks, since it generates all samples in one batch (§<a href="#S7.SS5" title="VII-E Q5: Runtime Overhead and Cost-Model Error ‣ VII Evaluation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VII-E</span></a>); and (3) the cost of each query must be known before it runs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST<span id="S5.SS2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-Online</span></span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online removes the offline phase.
It uses two kinds of feedback while it runs: the answers it has already generated for the current query, and the measured cost of the steps it has already executed.
Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ V-B ATEST-Online ‣ V ATESTDesign ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows the loop.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step-by-step sampling.</span>
<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online starts with <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
It then climbs the same ladder <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1\!\to\!3\!\to\!4\!\to\!6\!\to\!8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.484em;" width="0.484em"><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mpadded><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\!\to\!3\!\to\!4\!\to\!6\!\to\!8</annotation></semantics></math>, but it only generates the <em id="S5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">new</em> samples at each step.
Samples from earlier steps are kept and reused.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning signal: vote stability.</span>
After each step, <span id="S5.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online groups the answers and counts votes.
Let <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> be the current plurality answer after <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> samples.
The <em id="S5.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stability</em> is the chance that <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> would still win if we went all the way to <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\max}=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\max}=8</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(B)=P\big(w_{B}\text{ is still the plurality answer at }B_{\max}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is still the plurality answer at </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(B)=P\big(w_{B}\text{ is still the plurality answer at }B_{\max}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online estimates <math id="S5.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with a small Monte Carlo simulation of the remaining samples, based on the current vote counts.
The expected gain of the next step is the increase in stability:</p>
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta U=S_{\text{after}}-S_{\text{now}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>after</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mtext>now</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta U=S_{\text{after}}-S_{\text{now}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">This signal does not need the correct answer.
It only asks: <em id="S5.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">would more samples still change the result?</em></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Resource signal: online cost learning.</span>
After each executed step, <span id="S5.SS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online records the measured energy <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of that step and a feature vector <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> that describes the step (the number of new samples) and the current GPU state.
It predicts energy with a linear model, <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{E}=\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{E}=\boldsymbol{\theta}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and updates <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with the standard recursive least squares (RLS) rule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{k}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{k}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbf{P}_{t-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}}{\lambda+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{t-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbf{P}_{t-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}}{\lambda+\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{t-1}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t-1}+\mathbf{k}_{t}\big(e_{t}-\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t-1}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t-1}+\mathbf{k}_{t}\big(e_{t}-\boldsymbol{\theta}_{t-1}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{P}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{P}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{P}_{t-1}-\mathbf{k}_{t}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{t-1}\big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tfrac{1}{\lambda}\big(\mathbf{P}_{t-1}-\mathbf{k}_{t}\boldsymbol{\phi}_{t}^{\top}\mathbf{P}_{t-1}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> is a forgetting factor (<math id="S5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> means no forgetting).
RLS is cheap (a few small matrix operations per step), needs no training data, and starts learning from the first query.
Because measurements arrive after every step, the model quickly sees the effect of a load change.
A second RLS model predicts step latency in the same way.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Safety margin.</span>
To lower the risk of underestimating the cost, <span id="S5.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online uses a conservative estimate for the next step:</p>
<table id="S5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\mathrm{inc}}=\hat{E}+\beta\,\sigma_{E}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>inc</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>E</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\mathrm{inc}}=\hat{E}+\beta\,\sigma_{E},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is the uncertainty of the current prediction and <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> sets how careful the controller is.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Continue or stop.</span>
<span id="S5.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online continues only if the next step is worth its cost and fits in the budget:</p>
<table id="S5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta U}{E_{\mathrm{inc}}}\geq\gamma\quad\text{and}\quad E_{\mathrm{inc}}\leq E_{\mathrm{rem}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>inc</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>inc</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>rem</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta U}{E_{\mathrm{inc}}}\geq\gamma\quad\text{and}\quad E_{\mathrm{inc}}\leq E_{\mathrm{rem}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a minimum gain per joule and <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\mathrm{rem}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>rem</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\mathrm{rem}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the remaining energy budget.
It also stops when the answer is already stable, when more samples are unlikely to resolve a disagreement, or when it reaches <math id="S5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online for one query <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
