<div id="S7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup cost versus serving cost.</span>
Table <a href="#S7.T4" title="TABLE IV ‣ VII-C Q3: Energy Cost, Including Profiling ‣ VII Evaluation ‣ ATEST: Adaptive Resource-Aware Test-Time Scaling for LLM Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV</span></a> puts the full cost of both modes side by side.
<span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated must profile every dataset before it can serve a single query: 5.73 GPU-hours, 7.16 MJ, and 176,000 generated samples for our four datasets.
<span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online skips this stage completely and starts serving at once; its cost model learns during normal serving, so its learning cost is already inside the serving numbers.
Serving itself costs almost the same for both modes (about 0.14 hours and 0.15 MJ for 2,000 queries), but <span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online answers all 2,000 queries and gives 65 more correct answers.
In total, <span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated uses about 42<math id="S7.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> more GPU time and 48<math id="S7.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> more energy than <span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online in our study.
Calibration is a one-time cost per dataset, so a long, stable deployment can spread it over many queries, but it must be repeated whenever the model, the GPU, the prompt format, or the workload changes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Answer to Q3:</span> <span id="S7.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Online is the most energy-efficient mode on the long-answer datasets. Including profiling, it uses 42<math id="S7.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> less GPU time and 48<math id="S7.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> less energy than <span id="S7.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ATEST</span>-Calibrated for the same 2,000 queries.</p>
</div>
</section>
